> Thanks Ramesh.
> I was reserving and mapping buffers "every time". This was=20
> not required.
> I modified the code to reserve and map a buffer only once and=20
> use the mapped address for future.
> This modification reduced the overhead.
>=20
> I have one more doubt.
> Does DSP use virtual-to-physical mapping for all the=20
> addresses it accesses (including DSP's local buffers)?
> Or it uses this mapping only to access shared buffers?
> Wont it be a big overhead if DSP accesses all the memories=20
> through virtual-to-physical mapping?
>=20
> Regards,
> Viraj
>=20
>=20
